--   Partner addresses: the selected bit i of record j and the record with it set to b
-- statement:
--   **Partner addresses**: the selected bit `i` of record `j` and the record with it set to `b`.
--
--   The following holds (Lean statement, in the scope of module `Solutions.KFHKer`):
--
--   ```lean
--   theorem NLogN.KFH.layer_partner (hρ : ρ < K) (i : Fin D) {j : ℕ}
--       (hj : j < vol (Butterfly.layerShape P K D S)) (b : Fin 2) :
--       ((Butterfly.layerSel P K D S ρ hρ).bits (decode (Butterfly.layerShape P K D S) j) i : ℕ) =
--         j / stT K D S ρ i % 2 ∧
--       ((encode (Butterfly.layerShape P K D S) ((Butterfly.layerSel P K D S ρ hρ).set
--         (decode (Butterfly.layerShape P K D S) j)
--         (Function.update ((Butterfly.layerSel P K D S ρ hρ).bits
--           (decode (Butterfly.layerShape P K D S) j)) i b)) : ℕ) : ℤ) =
--         j + ((b : ℤ) - (j / stT K D S ρ i % 2 : ℕ)) * stT K D S ρ i
--   ```
--
--   **Context.** The lemma belongs to the part *KFH: an individual selected-bit kernel as one `qop` pass on a record array*: The layer layout of Proposition 14 is `[P] × [2^K]^D × [S]` (`Butterfly.layerShape`), records in
--   lexicographic order.  Bit `ρ` of chunk `i` has record stride `stT = 2^ρ · vol(suffix after
--   chunk i)`: the address with that bit flipped is `j ± stT` (`layer_partner`).  On the flat
--   Gaussian list (records of `r` coefficients) the paired entries are at distance `B1 = stT · r`,
--   in blocks of `2 B1`; this is exactly the two-stream pass `KFB.qop [M] B1 G` with
--   `G = P · 2^{K i} · 2^{K-ρ-1}` groups.
--
